<title>UK: MSAS first in at Chek Lap Kok.</title>
<headline>MSAS first in at Chek Lap Kok.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON</dateline>
<text>
<p>International freight forwarder MSAS Cargo International said it is the first management company to sign a letter of intent for space at Hong Kong's new airport, Chek Lap Kok.</p>
<p>MSAS added in a statement that it will invest four million stg in doubling its current office and warehouse capacity by taking more than 145,000 sq. ft. in the Airport Freight Forwarding Centre (AFFC) to be opened at the same time as the airport in April 1998.</p>
<p>MSAS is a member of the London-based Ocean Group Plc.</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
